Z||000000||mrfixit58||03-30-2001||01:02 PM||||A 1993 Caddy Siville with a Northstar! Local police auto auction. Retired narc car. I bid to $3250 and it sold for $3300. What scared me was the motor. THe coolant tank was empty and the buzz was the motor had a blown head gasket. <P>I asked the guy who bought it if he was going to fix it or part it. He said he may part it and took my phone number. I told him that I wanted the motor, tranny, wiring and computer. I got his card. We'll see.<P>I was so CLOSE!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"><P>Roy   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by mrfixit58 (edited 03-30-2001).]||||reg||9
Z||000001||StuGood||03-30-2001||01:38 PM||||You missed out on paying over $3000 for a car with a blown head gasket, eh?  Sounds good to me!<P>Soon a sweet little old lady will probably sell "a nice young man like you" her old Seville she never uses anymore for $500, and even drive it over to your place for you.<P>All I can say is, treat her nice, listen to all of her stories, and give her a lift back.  She'll be happy, you'll be happy, and such a deal  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> !        ||||reg||5
Z||000002||mrfixit58||03-30-2001||03:07 PM||||I forgot to mention that one of the guys wanted the body and custom wheels and had already told me that he would give me $2000. I called the Caddy dealer and the gasket set was $250. Considering these motors and trannys are going for $3000 in the bone yard, I thought I was on to something pretty good. Still do. <P>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||6
